hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15594","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, he said: Muayqib narrated to me, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Wiping in the mosque, meaning the pebbles. He said: So he said: If you must do, then one."
"15595","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Muayqib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"15596","He said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: Muayqib narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning a man levelling the dust where he prostrates: If you do, then one."
"15598","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah, from Muharrish al-Kabi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from al-Jiranah performing Umrah, entered Makkah by night, then went out within its night and morning came at al-Jiranah as spending the night. When the sun declined, he took in the belly of Sarif until the road joined, the road of Madinah. He said: Therefore his Umrah was hidden."
"15599","Rawh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim informed me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah, from Muharrish al-Kabi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, then he mentioned it."
